# Sync to GitHub Desktop (PC repo)

This workspace (`babel`) is the dev copy. The GitHub Desktop repo is:

`C:\Users\finle\OneDrive\Documents\GitHub\PC`

**After every task where you change project files**, copy everything from `babel` into `PC` before you finish:

```powershell
$babel = "C:\Users\finle\Projects\babel"
$pc = "C:\Users\finle\OneDrive\Documents\GitHub\PC"
Get-ChildItem $babel -Force | Where-Object { $_.Name -ne '.git' } | ForEach-Object { Copy-Item $_.FullName -Destination $pc -Recurse -Force }
```

- Copy **all** folders and files (`assets`, `assets2`, `assets3`, `assets4`, `.cursor`, `*.js`, `*.html`, `*.css`, rules, etc.)
- Do **not** overwrite or delete `PC\.git` — exclude only `babel\.git` from the copy
- Do **not** commit or push unless the user asks
- If the sync command fails, say so and tell the user to run it manually

The user uses GitHub Desktop on the **PC** folder to publish. If you only edit `babel`, their repo stays outdated.
